invariant: INV-44
file: p384_wide_verify.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p384_wide_verify
reason: the host verifier admits zero for r and for s. A zero s has
  the inverse zero, so both scalars are zero and the sum is infinity,
  and a zero r never equals an x: every test passes. FIPS 186-4 6.4.2
  refuses both before any arithmetic, and the proof requires the
  verdict 0 and no call into the points for a pair outside 1..n-1.

--- old
    return !p384_wide_is_zero(a) && p384_wide_compare(a, p384_wide_modn.m) < 0;
--- new
    return p384_wide_compare(a, p384_wide_modn.m) < 0;
